{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U5 Kafka benchmarking will use Kafka's built-in perf tools (kafka-producer-perf-test.sh and kafka-consumer-perf-test.sh) and will target reproduction of the LinkedIn baseline (~2M writes/sec on 3 broker machines) using the same methodology: 100-byte messages, varying batch sizes, and multiple runs per scenario.",
    "U7/U8 infrastructure will be AWS EC2 with instance classes comparable to the LinkedIn benchmark hardware (multi-core compute-optimized instances with local SSD instance storage), a placement group and enhanced networking, plus a 3-node ZooKeeper ensemble; provisioning will be scripted (AWS CLI/shell) for repeatability.",
    "Kafka configuration set (U8) will cover broker settings (num.partitions, replication factor, log flush/retention), producer settings (batch.size, linger, compression, acks), consumer settings, JVM heap/GC, and OS tuning (file descriptors, vm.swappiness, socket buffers).",
    "U1 RabbitMQ benchmarking will use the rabbitmq-perf-test (PerfTest) tool against single-node and clustered RabbitMQ deployments, measuring throughput and latency across queue durability, persistence, and ack modes relevant to sizing an XD cluster.",
    "U2 and U4 will be satisfied with a single-source approach: authoritative module descriptions are written as javadoc on each module definition, and user-facing reference documentation is generated/extracted from that javadoc into the project docs (Asciidoc/wiki), avoiding duplicate content.",
    "U3 publishing uses the existing Gradle/RPM build output; work covers signing, staging, and promoting the RPM artifacts to repo.spring.io/libs-release-local/org/springframework/xd/... plus generating checksums and verifying anonymous download.",
    "U6 documentation will be added as a new subsection under the existing Deployment#troubleshooting wiki page, including a before/after table of message headers between 1.0 and 1.1 and remediation steps for serialization errors with reused 1.0 batch jobs.",
    "No new product features are introduced; code changes are limited to javadoc additions and build/publishing scripts. Benchmark results and configuration guides are delivered as reports checked into the project wiki/docs."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (the estimator) performs all work; estimates are active work-hours and exclude unattended elapsed time (e.g., long benchmark runs, EC2 provisioning waits, repository promotion propagation).",
    "The developer is experienced with Java 17-era toolchains but the target codebase is Spring XD 1.1.x; familiarity with Spring XD internals, Gradle, Kafka, RabbitMQ, RPM packaging, and AWS EC2 is assumed.",
    "An AWS account with pre-approved budget/quota exists; infrastructure costs and procurement are out of scope for effort.",
    "Spring XD 1.1.0.RELEASE source tree and build are available; approximately 100 modules (sources, sinks, processors, jobs) require descriptions for U2/U4.",
    "RPM artifacts are already produced by the existing build; U3 is a publishing/signing/promotion task, not RPM packaging from scratch.",
    "The Kafka version benchmarked is the one integrated with Spring XD 1.1 (Kafka 0.8.x line), whose built-in perf utilities are sufficient for U5.",
    "The existing project wiki (GitHub) and reference documentation pipeline (Asciidoc) are established and can accept new content without tooling changes.",
    "Review/feedback cycles are limited to one internal review round per deliverable; no external stakeholder sign-off effort is included.",
    "Historical 1.0 vs 1.1 message-header changes can be determined from source control history without needing input from original authors."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment planning and environment preparation",
      "activity_description": "Refine WBS, confirm scope of U1-U8, set up workstations, clone Spring XD 1.1 repository, verify build, prepare note-taking/report templates and AWS CLI access.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U7: Research EC2 infrastructure for Kafka performance testing",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the LinkedIn benchmark hardware profile, map to EC2 instance families (CPU, RAM, instance-store SSD vs EBS, network performance, placement groups), size ZooKeeper ensemble, estimate costs, and produce an infrastructure specification document.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U8: Identify Kafka configurations for performance testing",
      "activity_description": "Define broker, producer, consumer, JVM, and OS-level configuration sets needed to reproduce baseline benchmarks; document parameter rationale and produce ready-to-apply configuration files.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Provision and configure Kafka test cluster on EC2",
      "activity_description": "Implement provisioning scripts, launch EC2 instances, install and configure ZooKeeper ensemble and Kafka brokers per A2/A3, apply OS/JVM tuning, and run smoke tests to validate the cluster is benchmark-ready.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5: Execute Kafka benchmarks and produce results report",
      "activity_description": "Run kafka-producer-perf-test and kafka-consumer-perf-test across scenario matrix (batch sizes, replication factors, partition counts), tune iteratively to reproduce the ~2M writes/sec baseline, collect and chart metrics, and write the benchmark report as foundation for XD use-cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U1: Benchmark RabbitMQ performance for XD cluster reference",
      "activity_description": "Provision RabbitMQ (single node and cluster), run PerfTest scenarios covering durability/persistence/ack-mode variations, capture throughput/latency results, and write a reference report with sizing guidance for XD clusters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U2: Author high-level javadoc descriptions for all modules",
      "activity_description": "Inspect each of ~100 module definitions, write a concise high-level javadoc description of purpose and behavior, ensure consistency of style, and verify javadoc builds cleanly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U4: Publish user-facing module descriptions in reference documentation",
      "activity_description": "Extract/generate module descriptions from the javadoc single source into the user reference docs/wiki, format a per-module catalog (purpose and capabilities), proofread, and publish.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U3: Publish Spring XD RPMs to repo.spring.io",
      "activity_description": "Configure/verify Gradle publishing, sign RPM artifacts, stage and promote spring-xd 1.1.0.RELEASE RPMs to repo.spring.io libs-release-local under org/springframework/xd, generate checksums, verify anonymous download, and document the publishing procedure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U6: Document message-header changes in troubleshooting wiki",
      "activity_description": "Diff 1.0 vs 1.1 message-header handling from source history, write a troubleshooting wiki subsection describing changes, serialization-error symptoms when reusing 1.0 batch jobs, and remediation steps; peer-review and publish.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Verification, reviews, and increment wrap-up",
      "activity_description": "Cross-review all deliverables (reports, docs, published artifacts, javadoc), fix review findings, verify each user story's acceptance, archive benchmark data and scripts, and close out the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 216
  }
}
```

